you know financing is always hard this
they started with a crowdfunding

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.380
campaign and grew and you know said we
had some initial funding come in but we

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.609
we were given deadlines and we kept
getting this deadline extended and I

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:28.349
needed to get more money in or we were
going to lose the funding we had so that

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:32.880
was a huge stress it was like a year and
or over a year of trying to raise more

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.320
money to actually you know be able to
shoot the film and for me as a producer

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.950
it was something you know this was new
territory to me I'd produce but I hadn't

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:46.050
gone out and raised money for a feature
before so you know and in LA everyone's

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.829
got a film that they think is great that
they're trying to get made so that was

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:53.760
really hard particularly because he had
these deadlines and at some point you

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.510
have to and you know I went to a lot of
producer seminars and people like you

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:01.620
know whatever budget you've got however
small have a big you're always gonna

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:06.930
want more just just shoot just shoot
scale it down do something but don't let

